  "configById": {
    "Markdown!l2qk5p": {
      "fontSize": 12,
      "markdown": "# **MAIN TAB**\r\n\r\n## **Nodes providing data and responding to this panel:**\r\n\r\n* Traxxas Node\r\n* Policy Node\r\n* Cone Detector Node\r\n\r\n## **Description of this tab:**\r\n\r\n* **COLUMN 1**:\r\n  * These butons are for enabling and disabling the Traxxas and Policy nodes.\r\n  * To test run the policy in the POlicy Node, click the buttons from top to bottom, which is:\r\n    1. Make the Policy Node publish \"zero\" values for the actions.\r\n    2. Enable the Traxxas Node to send actions through to the actual car.\r\n    3. Turn on the policy.\r\n    4. Stop the policy from publishing any actions.\r\n    5. Disable the Traxxas node, which means that it send neutral commands to the car regardless of what actions is might receive from the policy.\r\n    6. To enable manual driving, you need to put the Traxxas node into the \"disarmed\" state.\r\n\r\n* **COLUMN 2**:\r\n  * The coloured panels display:\r\n    * The state of the Traxxas Node.\r\n    * The state of the Policy Node.\r\n    * The validity of the signal from the RC remote channels (if this is BAD then mostly likely the car is turned off or the batteries are flat).\r\n\r\n* **COLUMN 3**:\r\n  * First plot: The (x,y) cone location data from the Detector Node. This data is in the coordinate frame of the car.\r\n  * Second plot: the drive and steering  commands that the Traxxas node is sending to the car (in normalized units).\r\n  * Third plot: the drive and steering commands being received as manual input from the RC remote (in normalized units).\r\n",
      "renderMode": "static"
    },
