    "Markdown!9qsjhw": {
      "fontSize": 12,
      "markdown": "# **IMAGE STREAMS TAB**\r\n\r\n## **Nodes providing data to this panel:**\r\n\r\n* Cone Detector\r\n\r\n## **Description of this tab:**\r\n\r\n* **IMPORTANT:** You should only stream images for debugging purposes.\r\n* Streaming images clogs up the WiFi bandwidth and makes everything run slower for you and for everyone else in the same room.\r\n* The most useful image for debugging is the \"bounding box image stream\" because it allows you to see what cones are or aren't being detected.\r\n* The \"plain image stream\" comes from the Stream Node.\r\n* The \"bounding box image stream\" and \"depth image stream\" come from the detector node.\r\n* For the \"bounding box image stream\" to work, launch with:\r\n```\r\ndream runtime start oakd_cone_detector --debug-images annotated\r\n```\r\n* For the \"depth image stream\" to work, launch with:\r\n```\r\ndream runtime start oakd_cone_detector --debug-images depth\r\n```\r\n",
      "renderMode": "static"
    },
