    "Markdown!4aawcqw": {
      "fontSize": 12,
      "markdown": "# **Wheel Speed Tab**\r\n\r\n## **Nodes providing data to this panel:**\r\n\r\n* Traxxas Node\r\n\r\n## **Description of this tab:**\r\n\r\n* This tab display the measurements from the wheel speed sensor.\r\n* The top plot is the wheel speed (in meters per second), which is based on an estimate of a wheel diameter of 10.5cm.\r\n* The bottom plot is the period of the encoder measurements (in seconds).\r\n* **Important:** At low speeds the encoder period can be 1 second (or higher), hence:\r\n  * The wheel speed estimator waits 3 seconds with no new encoder data before concluding that the wheels have stopped.\r\n  * At low speed, new measurements come is at approximately half the encoder period, hence, a policy for low-speed cruise-control must take this into account.",
      "renderMode": "static"
    },
